AGFTR2152G4,"Add contemporary style, safely, to kitchens, bathrooms and more, with GFCI Outlets from the adorne Collection. Meeting Electrical Code* for ground fault protection in the home, GFCI outlets make it easier to fix trips right where they happen â€“ no more confusion or running to the breaker box. The adorne GFCI Outlets also self-test automatically every three seconds to ensure reliable protection from shock due to ground fault occurrences. *GFCI protection is required by code in bathrooms, kitchens, garages, basements, outdoor areas, and for any other outlets found within six feet of a sink or water source. GFCI outlets should always be used when replacing existing GFCI outlets during renovation.Made exclusively for use with screwless Wall Plates from the adorneÂ® Collection, sold separately."
