1597TRA,"GFCI outlets from the radiantÂ® Collection self-test automatically every three seconds to ensure reliable protection from shock due to ground fault occurrences. Meeting National Electrical Code for ground fault protection in the home, GFCI outlets make it easier to fix trips right where they happen â€“ no more confusion or running to the breaker box. This model includes an optional audible alarm, so trips never go unnoticed, and is great for appliances where loss of power could cause damage, such as freezers and sump pumps. Maximize safety, in style, with GFCI protection featuring the sleek, clean lines of radiant.GFCI protection is required by code in bathrooms, kitchens, garages, basements, outdoor areas, and for any other outlets found within six feet of a sink or water source. GFCI outlets should always be used when replacing existing GFCI outlets during renovation.Made exclusively for use with screwless Wall Plates from the radiantÂ® Collection, sold separately."
